  "articleBody": "Ever wonder why your plumbing project hits snags, causing delays and headaches? It often boils down to a few common mistakes that are totally avoidable with some savvy coordination. For starters, trying to get the plumber in before prerequisite work is finished is a classic. You can't put the cart before the horse! Another big one is not confirming potential conflicts with other trades, like electrical or HVAC. Imagine two essential systems trying to occupy the same space—that's a recipe for rework. People also frequently underestimate fixture lead times or how long inspections take, which can really throw off your whole schedule. And, of course, failing to document changes in writing? That's just asking for misunderstandings down the road. If your project involves multiple trades, tight sequencing, or any work that touches permits and inspections, having a pro coordinate things can make a huge difference. HH Remodeling LLC knows how to keep things moving so your plumbing work gets done right and on time. We'll make sure everyone's on the same page.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}